== Leveling ==
{{:SkyBlock Levels/UI/Leveling}}

The player gains {{DarkAqua|1 SkyBlock Level}} for every {{SkyBlock XP|100}} they have.

The player can complete a wide variety of tasks to gain {{SkyBlock XP}}. Tasks can only be completed once.

{{:SkyBlock Levels/Tasks}}

== Trivia ==
*For a while on December 7th, 2022 there was a bug where Vanilla [[Experience]] would give {{SkyBlock XP|1}}. The player's '''SkyBlock Level''' would exceed the cap of 500, and go instead up to {{Rmt|&8[&494949&8]}} if the player would have maxed Vanilla experience levels. 
**Levels above 500 gave 0 level stats, the same as a level 0 player would get
**It was also possible to get a level 0 if player would spend their experience.
*{{RankName|MVP+|Celatrix|plus_color=0}} (better known as DeathStreeks) and {{RankName|MVP++|15h|plus_color=0}}, who both had  competed for first place for nearly a year since their release in September 28, 2022 until September 19, 2023 where they both maxed the requirement at the time.
*Until April 28, 2026, reaching {{Forest Whispers|2,147,483,647}} would result in an overflow, providing a negative amount of {{SkyBlock Experience}}. The player's '''SkyBlock Level''' would therefore go negative.
**{{RankName|MVP++|Preposing}} was the first person to reach this amount, resulting in a '''SkyBlock Level''' of {{Rmt|&8[&7-8461&8]}} and lower. 
**Getting a negative '''SkyBlock Level''' will convert the {{Item|Book of Progression}} to {{Common}} and block every level-related feature ([[Bazaar]], [[Rift]], etc.)
**This was patched in the 0.24.4 update, adding a hard cap of {{Forest Whispers|2,000,000,000}}.

